  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "2fe016c4-af2a-404a-a12b-0bd7cfab6ce9",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1824,
        1536
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Construction Incident Photo \u2192 Verified Report\n### How it works\n\n1. Receives an incident report submission with an uploaded image through an n8n form trigger.\n2. Extracts image metadata and evaluates authenticity using an external AI image check API.\n3. Sends an immediate Slack alert if the submitted image is flagged as suspicious.\n4. Uses a Gemini-backed AI agent to analyze incident details and parse structured output.\n5. Formats the evaluation results, posts a comprehensive report to Slack, and appends a log entry to Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Configure Google Gemini API credentials in the Gemini Chat Model node.\n- - [ ] Set up Slack credentials and select the target channels for notifications and reports.\n- - [ ] Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the target spreadsheet and worksheet.\n- - [ ] Verify the API credentials and URL configured in the Post to Image Check API node.\n- - [ ] Share or embed the n8n form trigger link to begin collecting incident reports.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the authenticity score thresholds in the Check If Image is Suspicious node or update the Gemini agent prompt to tailor damage assessment categories."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "154646d6-aed2-49f1-ad71-86cfba069076",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
